    "services": "Real PostgreSQL, SQLite and Redis qualification on Windows; services may run natively or in a suitable local VM. Database/schema/role/environment setup remains required.",
    "isolation": "Qualify the selected backend on the Windows host or an optional VM. No automatic equivalence between native Windows protections and Linux seccomp/Landlock/KVM. Unqualified executable effects remain disabled; generated/untrusted code still requires qualified VM isolation.",
    "acceptance": "Preserve architecture, authorization, tenant isolation, budget, audit, cancellation, durability and test assertions. A platform decision is not executed acceptance evidence.",
    "runtimeImplementation": "Linux execution/deployment artifacts removed. Native Windows identity restart tests exist; executable Windows sandbox is explicitly unavailable until Task12 qualifies it.",
    "implementationRule": "Continue Windows task implementation without waiting for Linux; preserve real owner dependencies and security/runtime acceptance. A conditional future VM feature cannot block unrelated Windows work."
